-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Support for Israel — the issue vertical's roll-call record, 117th-119th Congress
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Generated by scripts/vr-gen-israel-vote-migration.mjs from db/vr-israel-vote-seed.json.
-- Do not hand-edit: regenerate, or roll forward with a new migration.
--
-- 16 roll calls · 415 attributed member votes · 16 measures
--
-- The issue key israel_support was added because U.S. support for Israel was being scored
-- through four general-posture chips that none of the underlying statements or votes were
-- actually about. The chip has no votes behind it until this migration lands, and a chip
-- with no votes ranks nobody, so this is the record that makes it scoreable.
--
-- Direction is coded against the chip's own sentence — 'Keep backing Israel with U.S.
-- security aid, weapons and sanctions on its adversaries'. Seven measures are yea_supports
-- (the supplementals, the Jerusalem embassy limitation, the delivery mandate) and nine are
-- yea_opposes (the Arms Export Control Act disapproval resolutions and the Massie defund
-- amendment). Both directions are cross-party, which is why the key carries no `lean`.
--
-- Two non-passage question forms appear here and nowhere else in the ingest:
--   · 'On Agreeing to the Amendment' — an amendment has no passage vote, so agreeing to it
--     is its disposition. 28 amendment roll calls already sit on this footing.
--   · 'On the Motion to Discharge' — under the Arms Export Control Act's expedited
--     procedure a disapproval resolution the Foreign Relations Committee has not reported
--     reaches the floor only by discharge, and none has ever carried. The discharge vote is
--     the entire Senate record on the arms sale, not a step toward a later vote.
-- scripts/test-vr-vote-seed.mjs gates each form on the measure's shape and requires the
-- seed to carry a written decisiveWhy, so neither widens into a loophole.
--
-- Slicing: H.R. 8034 carries the Israel reading of the 2024 supplemental, not H.R. 815.
-- The enacted package (P.L. 118-50) bundled Israel with Ukraine, the Indo-Pacific, TikTok
-- divest-or-ban and fentanyl sanctions; the House voted its divisions separately, and this
-- is the one that asked about Israel alone (366-58). H.R. 815 keeps its five existing keys
-- and gains no israel_support row, exactly as H.R. 8035 already carries the Ukraine side.
--
-- Attribution is fail-closed. House rolls resolve by the bioguide id in the Clerk's XML;
-- Senate rolls carry no bioguide, so senators resolve by (last name, state) against
-- db/vr-member-map.json and only on a unique hit. Unrecognised or ambiguous members are
-- skipped and counted, never guessed. totals is the FULL chamber tally and is_party is
-- computed from the full recorded vote before the roster filter, so a 63-member roster
-- cannot invent a margin or a party crossover.
--
-- Idempotent: every write is guarded. H.Amdt. 235's measure, roll call and 38 member votes
-- are already live and land as no-ops; only its new israel_support mapping is a real write.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

